# Logging

## Framework semantics

CakePHP `Log` is configured with scopes/engines in config. Application code should log through `Log::` / injected loggers — not `echo`/`var_dump` in production paths.

## Required behavior

- Configure log engines/levels in config for the environment.
- Log failures with enough context to debug; never log passwords, tokens, or full card data.
- Prefer structured context arrays over string concatenation of sensitive objects.
- Do not leave debug logging that dumps entities with hidden fields in production.

## Anti-patterns

- Logging secrets or session identifiers casually
- `var_dump` / `debug()` left in committed hot paths
- Inventing Monolog service providers as a CakePHP default when Log suffices

## Review checklist

- [ ] Errors are logged where operators expect
- [ ] No secrets in log lines
- [ ] Production log level is appropriate
